# ==============================================================================
# 14_singularity_avoidance.scara - Central Singularity & Dead Zone Detour Routing
# ==============================================================================
# Demonstrates trajectory execution transferring between opposite work zones
# across the robot cell while safely bypassing the central base singularity dead zone.
#
# SCARA Kinematic Workspace Constraints:
# - Mechanical Inner Dead Zone: R_min = 77.6 mm (J2 folded limit 150 deg).
# - Base Singularity:          At origin (0.0, 0.0) where Jacobian loses rank.
# - Safe Annular Reach:        77.6 mm <= R <= 295.0 mm.
#
# Scenario:
# 1. P1_WORK: Work point in positive quadrant (X=60.0, Y=140.0, Z=20.0).
# 2. P1_LIFT: Tool lift to clearance height (Z=40.0).
# 3. Direct linear move to target P2 (X=60.0, Y=-140.0) would pass through
#    (X=60.0, Y=0.0) where R=60.0 mm < R_min (77.6 mm), crashing into the inner
#    mechanical dead zone / singularity.
# 4. Safe Trajectory Detour:
#    - Routes outward along tangential clearance waypoints at R ~ 150-160 mm:
#      DETOUR_1: (X=140.0, Y=60.0, Z=40.0, R=152.3 mm)
#      DETOUR_2: (X=160.0, Y=0.0, Z=40.0, R=160.0 mm)
#      DETOUR_3: (X=140.0, Y=-60.0, Z=40.0, R=152.3 mm)
#    - Approaches target in negative quadrant: P2_LIFT (X=60.0, Y=-140.0, Z=40.0).
#    - Lowers tool to destination work point: P2_WORK (X=60.0, Y=-140.0, Z=20.0).
# ==============================================================================

ENABLE
HOME

SPEED WORK 40.0
SPEED RAPID 120.0

# 1. Initial work operation in Zone A
MOVE_L X=60.0 Y=140.0 Z=20.0 PHI=0.0

# 2. Lift to safe clearance height
MOVE_L X=60.0 Y=140.0 Z=40.0 PHI=0.0

# 3. Tangential detour around inner singularity (R >= 150 mm > R_min 77.6 mm)
MOVE_L X=140.0 Y=60.0 Z=40.0 PHI=0.0
MOVE_L X=160.0 Y=0.0 Z=40.0 PHI=0.0
MOVE_L X=140.0 Y=-60.0 Z=40.0 PHI=0.0

# 4. Align above destination Zone B
MOVE_L X=60.0 Y=-140.0 Z=40.0 PHI=0.0

# 5. Descent to final work point in Zone B
MOVE_L X=60.0 Y=-140.0 Z=20.0 PHI=0.0
